Fix: the window repainted non-stop (600+ times per second) for the whole session

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0006-idle-overlay-no-continuous-repaint.patch
Status:     local patch, not upstream yet (small, general: worth proposing)

WHAT BROKE
  ImGuiDrawer::Draw asks the presenter for another UI-thread repaint after
  every paint as long as ANY ImGui dialog is open ("repaint and handle input
  continuously"). ReXApp::LaunchModule creates the achievement toast dialog
  (AchievementToastDialog, an ImGuiDialog) at launch and keeps it for the
  whole session, although it draws nothing until an achievement pops. So the
  window repainted in a loop from start to exit, each time showing the same
  guest frame, and with the Vulkan presenter's immediate present mode (no
  vsync) as fast as the GPU allowed. That's GPU time taken from the emulator
  (and our native renderer), and frame counters that watch presents
  (MangoHud) showed the repaint rate instead of the game's frame rate.

HOW WE FOUND IT (2026-09-26)
  A playtest with MangoHud and --fps_cap=180 showed 600+ fps in
  some areas. The game's own frame counter (the native renderer's periodic
  log line: game frame number + timestamp) said 59.4 frames per second all
  along. Reading the presenter: guest output refreshes request one paint
  each; the extra paints came from ImGuiDrawer's continuous request, and the
  only dialog open without any overlay shown was the achievement toast.

THE FIX
  ImGuiDialog::WantsContinuousRepaint() (default true: interactive overlays
  such as F3/F4/console keep today's behaviour). AchievementToastDialog says
  true only while a toast is queued or showing. ImGuiDrawer requests the
  continuous repaint only if some open dialog wants it. The idle toast is
  still drawn: every guest output refresh repaints the window once (the
  presenter's kUIThreadOnRequest path), which also starts a new toast.
  Measured after: MangoHud 52.8 fps average over a loading screen + gameplay,
  matching the game's own count (59.4 in gameplay).
---
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h b/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h
index a7ab6b3..d26525a 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/imgui_dialog.h
@@ -39,6 +39,14 @@ class ImGuiDialog {
 
   void Draw();
 
+  // Whether the window must keep repainting while this dialog is open (for
+  // animations and input). Most dialogs are interactive overlays and say yes.
+  // A dialog that is open all the time but usually shows nothing (the
+  // achievement toast) says no while idle; otherwise the window repaints
+  // continuously for the whole session, as fast as the GPU allows with the
+  // immediate present mode, instead of once per guest frame.
+  virtual bool WantsContinuousRepaint() const { return true; }
+
  protected:
   ImGuiDialog(ImGuiDrawer* imgui_drawer);
 
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.h b/include/rex/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.h
index 7642601..f3457b5 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.h
@@ -35,6 +35,9 @@ class AchievementToastDialog : public AchievementNotificationDialog {
   // Thread-safe: safe to call from any thread, including guest threads.
   void Push(const rex::system::AchievementEvent& event) override;
 
+  // Only while a toast is queued or showing (see ImGuiDialog).
+  bool WantsContinuousRepaint() const override;
+
  protected:
   void OnDraw(ImGuiIO& io) override;
 
@@ -47,7 +50,7 @@ class AchievementToastDialog : public AchievementNotificationDialog {
     std::optional<std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point> visible_since;
   };
 
-  std::mutex mutex_;
+  mutable std::mutex mutex_;
   std::deque<PendingToast> queue_;
   AchievementIconCache icon_cache_;
 };
diff --git a/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp b/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp
index f270f3c..92c431c 100644
--- a/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/imgui_drawer.cpp
@@ -439,7 +439,16 @@ void ImGuiDrawer::Draw(UIDrawContext& ui_draw_context) {
   if (!dialogs_.empty()) {
     // Repaint (and handle input) continuously if still active. In detached mode
     // there is no presenter; the app drives repaint via its own present loop.
-    if (presenter_) {
+    // Idle dialogs don't count: the guest output refresh still repaints the
+    // window once per guest frame, which draws them too.
+    bool continuous = false;
+    for (const ImGuiDialog* dialog : dialogs_) {
+      if (dialog->WantsContinuousRepaint()) {
+        continuous = true;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    if (presenter_ && continuous) {
       presenter_->RequestUIPaintFromUIThread();
     }
   }
diff --git a/src/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.cpp b/src/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.cpp
index 53b8c0b..0dbef1c 100644
--- a/src/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,11 @@ void AchievementToastDialog::Push(const rex::system::AchievementEvent& event) {
   queue_.push_back({event, std::chrono::steady_clock::now()});
 }
 
+bool AchievementToastDialog::WantsContinuousRepaint() const {
+  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
+  return !queue_.empty();
+}
+
 void AchievementToastDialog::OnDraw(ImGuiIO& io) {
   auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
 
